// currently inside a constrained arithmetic span in `insideConstrainedOut`, and
// the contents of the active span in `currentConstrainedOut`. Outside spans it
// generates freely, but if the delimiter token "<<" is competitive with the
// current argmax or if the chosen token itself contains "<<", it opens a span
// eagerly so arithmetic can be forced into delimiter form.
// Inside a span, the strategy distinguishes three cases: if the parser already
// accepts the current constrained prefix as complete, it closes with ">>"; if
// the parser is near a dead end or has very few valid continuations, it uses a
// hard constrained step; otherwise it boosts a small set of top valid tokens
// and samples, appending only parser-valid samples. This tracked state ensures
// that text between delimiters remains a parser-valid arithmetic computation
// while the outer text can still be generated naturally step by step.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
