// parser_validity: In the unconstrained branch, appending a normal token keeps
//   insideConstrainedOut false, so the implication is vacuous; opening a span
//   sets currentConstrainedOut := [], and parser.IsValidPrefix([]) holds by
//   precondition. In the complete-prefix branch, CloseConstrainedSpan sets
//   insideConstrainedOut to false, again making the implication vacuous. In the
//   hard constrained branch, ConstrainedStep is used only for an active valid
//   prefix and AppendConstrainedToken extends it with a valid next token. In
//   the soft constrained branch, we call AppendConstrainedToken only when
//   IsTokenValidNext says the sampled token is valid; the rejection sub-branch
//   leaves state unchanged.
// suffix: In the unconstrained non-opening sub-branch, currentConstrainedOut is
//   unchanged and empty because we are outside a span; in the opening
//   sub-branch, we append "<<" (or a token containing "<<") to generated and
//   set currentConstrainedOut := [], so the length-0 suffix matches []. In the
//   complete-prefix branch, CloseConstrainedSpan appends the closing delimiter
//   and resets currentConstrainedOut to []. In both constrained append
//   branches, AppendConstrainedToken appends the same token to generated and to
//   currentConstrainedOut; in the rejection branch nothing changes.
// cost: The unconstrained raw-sampling branch uses GenerateLogits plus
//   ChooseNextTokenUnconstrained, so we manually increment helpers.cost once
//   and also increment steps once. CloseConstrainedSpan bumps helpers.cost
//   internally and we increment steps once. The hard constrained branch uses
//   ConstrainedStep, which bumps helpers.cost internally, followed by a
//   non-bumping AppendConstrainedToken, and again steps increases by 1. The
//   soft constrained branch uses only non-bumping queries plus one primitive
//   ChooseNextTokenUnconstrained, after which we manually bump helpers.cost and
//   increment steps once; the rejection sub-branch does not change helpers.cost.
// progress: Each iteration increments steps by exactly 1 in every non-break
//   branch. The unconstrained branch appends at most one token. The
//   complete-prefix branch appends only the closing delimiter token. The hard
//   and soft constrained append branches append at most one token, while the
//   soft rejection branch appends none. Therefore |generated| grows by at most
//   one per step, so |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps is preserved.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

var steps := 0;

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
