// immediately closes with `>>`. Otherwise it asks the parser for the number of
// valid next tokens and whether the prefix is near a dead end. If there are no
// valid continuations, or the prefix is complete, it closes as soon as allowed;
// if continuation is possible, it uses `ConstrainedStep` to obtain a parser-
// valid next token. Because `ConstrainedStep` is only used while inside a span
// and every nonterminal constrained iteration either appends one valid token or
// closes the span, the method avoids leaving `<<` unterminated.
// 
// This change directly targets the evaluation failure mode: constrained spans
// now arise only from an actual emitted opening delimiter, and once active they
// are driven toward either valid completion plus `>>` closure or immediate stop
// on EOS, never left hanging by speculative opening logic.
